<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22925" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γύᾰλον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], τό</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hollow</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> always of the <i>breast-</i> or <i>back-piece</i> of the
			cuirass, [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θώρηκα] γυάλοισιν ἀρηρότα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.530
				</span></i>
			: sg., usu. of the <i>front-piece</i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.99
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hollow</i> of a vessel, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρατήρων γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					1052
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <i>hollow vessel</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοῦ γέμοντα γύαλα θησαυροὺς βροτῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1093
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοίλας πέτρας γ.</span>
			<i>hollow</i> of a rock, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1081
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>cavern</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρινα [μύχατα] γύαλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					189
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> pl., of
				<i>hollow ground, vales, dells</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυάλοις ὕπο Παρνησοῖο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					499
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				396
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νύσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					26.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. Θεράπνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					10.56
				</span></i>
			 (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. Πυθῶνος, Φοίβου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>P.</u>
					8.63
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				237
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ion</u>
				245
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				460
			</span></i>, may perh. refer to the rock-chambers of Delphi, cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γύαλα: θησαυροί, ταμιεῖα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, and so perh. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1093
			</span></i> (v. supr.)); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύδιά τ᾽ ἂγ
			γύαλα</span> throughout <i>the vales</i> of Lydia, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				550
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γύαλα χώρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					110
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθέρια γύαλα</span>
			<i>the vault</i> of heaven, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.281
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				19.16
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
